//       prot_set_propagation_p[p, i, o]      : Operand       one program-order step at instruction i
//       prot_flow_p[p]                       : Operand->Operand  dataflow edges protection follows
//                                                            to a transmitter in the final check
//   (3) leakage_function                     : Operand       what can transmit (one line)
//   plus optional contract side-condition facts, each tagged in the block.
//   Hooks the block may READ (all perturbation-aware): nonspeculative_p,
//   nonspeculative_xmit_p, spec_loads_p, after_unresolved_p and its four
//   instances, fed_p / unfed_p, ops_of, the *_p operand fields, rf_p, ddi_p,
//   op_edges_p, o_p, i_p, committed_p / resolved_p / ..., spo_p.
//   The block must NOT read the unperturbed program (Instruction., rf, ddi, spo,
